<http://data.silknow.org/event/198d81d2-4725-371e-a612-b69e7291dba8>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Alterations: Moderate alterations and additions were made for fancy dress in the late 19th century, which have been removed or reversed.\n\nHistorical significance: The pattern of the silk is representative of a new three-dimensional approach that developed in the early 1730s.  The very short sleeves of the mantua correspond to the period circa 1736-1739; similar examples appear in portraiture.\n\nRF number is 1985/1851."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/4d3bdec4-48eb-35df-adf6-8b475392368d> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Gladys Windsor Fry" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0191de84-2b1f-362a-9ac3-89bc7b09c2f6> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Alterations: Moderate alterations and additions were made for fancy dress in the late 19th century, which have been removed or reversed.\n\nHistorical significance: The pattern of the silk is representative of a new three-dimensional approach that developed in the early 1730s.  The very short sleeves of the mantua correspond to the period circa 1736-1739; similar examples appear in portraiture.\n\nRF number is 1985/1851."@en .

